ome/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33728" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+9{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+9{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33728" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa"} {"question" "q-33728" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33728" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡2t+3{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡2t+9{cos}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡2t+9{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+9{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡2t+9{cos}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33728" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+9{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-127419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ from $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-127419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-127419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa"} {"question" "q-127419" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-127419" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡t+9}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{3{cos}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+16}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-127419" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/10ee30ddf508bf985e1c3a41491818723b57301412a5514e4a39c3bc13518acd.png)\n\nWhich integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,2-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=\\pi ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa"} {"question" "q-33706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)={e}^{t}(\\,i+2\\,j+t\\,k)$ from  $t=1$ to $t=2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t{e}^{t})\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\,i+2{e}^{t}\\,j+(t{e}^{t}+{e}^{t})\\,k \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{({e}^{t})^{2}+(2{e}^{t})^{2}+({e}^{t}(t+1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+4{e}^{2t}+{e}^{2t}({t}^{2}+2t+1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}(1+4+{t}^{2}+2t+1)} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}(t+2)\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+2}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+4}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+5}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33862" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/e6de928031610e2aaf55e3dd753449f766e7dc028a6618087e7489224a73ea7d.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t+{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa"} {"question" "q-77070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-127573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/162c0d0310cbbb533c30af373820751fc6c5a447127958486571224d7f8ac07a.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ from $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-127573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & ={e}^{t}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|{e}^{t}|\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{2({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{e}^{t}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-127573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa"} {"question" "q-127573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-127573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2({e}^{\\pi }-1)"] ["math" "2{e}^{\\pi /2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi /2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi }-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-127573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/2efa774a3a7e97c23f695cfbdf681b53df055b8a84b84e2729af0a565841aeb7.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$\nfrom  $t=1$ to $t=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,,4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)}^{2}+{(4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t>0$ for $t\\in [1,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2(4-1) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa"} {"question" "q-77220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/b614e2c3e6abf0d7ddb8399aa7ea78b7a0e618a965ee7b5481edf08310a45031.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨{t}^{3}-3t,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩$ from $t=1$ to $t=2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-3,\\,6t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2}-3)^{2}+(6t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}-18{t}^{2}+9+36{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+18{t}^{2}+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2}+3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{t}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({t}^{3}+3t){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(8+6)-(1+3) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa"} {"question" "q-77065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "21"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/54cd1a0532bbdbe76bd81d5ad737f6d3e9f5293d08ea78758865b3b71850e346.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2},\\,2t⟩$ from $t=1$ to $t=e.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t}-t,\\,2⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{t}-t)}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-2+{t}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+2+{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{t}+t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}+t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{1}{t}+t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2})-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}-0-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}+1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa"} {"question" "q-77068" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77068" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}+{e}^{2}-2"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2}+1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}"] ["math" "{e}^{2}+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77068" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{2}+1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2},\\,2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,3t,\\,4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}+(3t)^{2}+{(4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡2t+9{t}^{2}+16{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}+9{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =5t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}5t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{5{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa"} {"question" "q-76914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,4,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(2t)}^{2}+0+{(2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\,t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2\\sqrt{2}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom $t=1$ to $t=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\sqrt{3}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{3}t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3}t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)+3{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t>0$ for $t\\in [1,3].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={t}^{2}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =9-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa"} {"question" "q-33779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "8\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "8\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-33779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨10,\\,\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(10),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,{t}^{2}-1,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+{(2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2}+1+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{({t}^{2}+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+t)|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =9+3-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa"} {"question" "q-77064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-77064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3}⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2t,\\,2{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(2t)}^{2}+{(2{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}+4{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(1+2{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =1+2{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(1+2{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(t+\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3})|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =3+18-0 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "709af184d805f83ffe8fcf8cf1aec878f4459116c29d8589faa971d65e2952fa"} {"question" "q-76908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "19"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "24"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "q-76908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "21"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/state.json" "file_sha256" "0b43e8de4a0065bb333a753d3c7cb9d0390d7d8305f4d18c659b51c073d29cad"} {"question" "e-3063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write down the integral that gives the arc length of the curve  $\\mathbf f (t) = \\langle 3 \\sin t, \\: 2\\sin 2t \\rangle$\nfrom $t =\\dfrac {3\\pi} 2$  to $t = 2\\pi.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/574a16e843a9c81e5fc9ddbbe2c0dc2c308ffcac4991bcbf48c7f45b4871c93b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/example-3063.json" "file_sha256" "c92f14e064fc67570e97c548727103230652186a36234e730b7b946cab910c7d"} {"question" "e-3063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf f'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡2t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/example-3063.json" "file_sha256" "c92f14e064fc67570e97c548727103230652186a36234e730b7b946cab910c7d"} {"question" "e-3064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf g (t) = \\langle 3 - 2 \\sin 2t, \\: 1 - 2\\cos 2t \\rangle$ from $t=\\dfrac \\pi 3$ to $\\pi.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/29c97e5963d451cc389944ef113764b2d15998448e773a02bb98c062207c2860.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/example-3064.json" "file_sha256" "aae1c10fbda307e8c5760f1441a9d730884b8f1469d948f741aaa6017649ceaa"} {"question" "e-3064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf g'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡2t+16{sin}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4t\\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =4(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/example-3064.json" "file_sha256" "aae1c10fbda307e8c5760f1441a9d730884b8f1469d948f741aaa6017649ceaa"} {"question" "e-6303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/8573aedcd26cba038b2db072560cd3d6ba7676542888a2d9b8a356713eaf6724.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf r (t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\: \\cos t, \\: t \\rangle$\nfrom  $t =0$ to $t = 2\\pi.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/example-6303.json" "file_sha256" "f326828e097bec933b49faf962a5b56f5ae069cf725d748e457efd34d13d2335"} {"question" "e-6303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\text{ }\\sqrt{2}\\,t{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(2\\pi -0) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/example-6303.json" "file_sha256" "f326828e097bec933b49faf962a5b56f5ae069cf725d748e457efd34d13d2335"}] "usage" {"q-33779" [] "e-3064" [] "e-6303" [] "e-3063" [] "q-33862" [] "q-33728" [] "q-77065" []} "basis" 1765 "retractions" [[17592186120205 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1837/Source/Images/q-33728.png)\n\nWhich integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{g} ( t ) = \\langle  \\sin   2 t , \\, \\cos   3 t \\rangle$ from $t = 0$ to $t = \\pi $?"] [17592186120205 :question/worked-solution "Differentiate to get $\\mathbf g'(t)=\\langle2\\cos(2t),-3\\sin(3t)\\rangle$. Its magnitude is $\\sqrt{4\\cos^2(2t)+9\\sin^2(3t)}$. Thus $$L=\\int_0^\\pi\\sqrt{4\\cos^2(2t)+9\\sin^2(3t)}\\,dt.$$"] [17592186120214 :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{f} ( t ) = {e}^{t} ( \\, \\mathbf{i} + 2 \\, \\mathbf{j} + t \\, \\mathbf{k} )$ from $t = 1$ to $t = 2$?"] [17592186120214 :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf f(t)=\\langle e^t,2e^t,te^t\\rangle$. The product rule gives $\\mathbf f'(t)=e^t\\langle1,2,t+1\\rangle$, so $\\|\\mathbf f'(t)\\|=e^t\\sqrt{1+4+(t+1)^2}$. Therefore $$L=\\int_1^2e^t\\sqrt{t^2+2t+6}\\,dt.$$"] [17592186120214 :question/difficulty 17592186045465] [17592186120454 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1837/Source/Images/q-77065.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{g} ( t ) = \\langle  {t}^{3} - 3 t , \\, 3 {t}^{2} \\rangle$ from $t = 1$ to $t = 2$?"] [17592186120454 :question/worked-solution "The velocity is $\\mathbf g'(t)=\\langle3t^2-3,6t\\rangle$. Its speed simplifies to $$\\|\\mathbf g'(t)\\|=3\\sqrt{(t^2-1)^2+4t^2}=3\\sqrt{(t^2+1)^2}=3(t^2+1).$$ Hence $$L=\\int_1^2 3(t^2+1)\\,dt=[t^3+3t]_1^2=14-4=10.$$"] [17592186120454 :question/difficulty 17592186045465] [17592186120208 :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{f} ( t ) = \\langle \\cos   t + t \\sin   t , \\, \\sin   t - t \\cos   t , \\, \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} {t}^{2} \\rangle$\n\nfrom $t = 1$ to $t = 3$."] [17592186120208 :question/worked-solution "The product rule gives $\\mathbf f'(t)=\\langle t\\cos t,t\\sin t,\\sqrt3t\\rangle$. For $1\\le t\\le3$, its magnitude is $\\sqrt{t^2(\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t+3)}=2t$. Hence $$L=\\int_1^3 2t\\,dt=[t^2]_1^3=9-1=8.$$"] [17592186119486 :question/problem "Write down the integral that gives the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf f (t) = \\langle 3 \\sin t, \\: 2\\sin 2t \\rangle$\nfrom $t =\\dfrac {3\\pi} 2$ to $t = 2\\pi$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1837/Source/Images/0c0c2dffe8d85c38943e919e899e3373.png)"] [17592186119486 :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf f'(t)\\|$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{\\prime }(t) &= \\langle \\frac{d}{dt}(3\\sin t), \\frac{d}{dt}(2\\sin 2t)\\rangle  \\\\\n&= \\langle 3\\cos t, 4\\cos 2t\\rangle  \\\\\n\\Vert f^{\\prime }(t)\\Vert  &= \\sqrt{(3\\cos t)^{2} + (4\\cos 2t)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9\\cos^{2} t + 16\\cos^{2} 2t}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL &= \\int _{a}^{b}\\Vert f^{\\prime }(t)\\Vert dt \\\\\n&= \\int _{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{9\\cos^{2} t + 16\\cos^{2} 2t}dt\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119487 :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf g (t) = \\langle 3 - 2 \\sin 2t, \\: 1 - 2\\cos 2t \\rangle$ from $t=\\dfrac \\pi 3$ to $\\pi$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1837/Source/Images/bfcb501a54f7ab19db15a4c4726f7f63.png)"] [17592186119487 :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf g'(t)\\|$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ng^{\\prime }(t) &= \\langle \\frac{d}{dt}(3 - 2\\sin 2t), \\frac{d}{dt}(1 - 2\\cos 2t)\\rangle  \\\\\n&= \\langle  - 4\\cos 2t, 4\\sin 2t\\rangle  \\\\\n\\Vert g^{\\prime }(t)\\Vert  &= \\sqrt{(-4\\cos 2t)^{2} + (4\\sin 2t)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16\\cos^{2} 2t + 16\\sin^{2} 2t} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16} \\\\\n&= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL &= \\int _{a}^{b}\\Vert g^{\\prime }(t)\\Vert dt \\\\\n&= \\int _{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }4dt \\\\\n&= 4t \\mid _{\\pi /3}^{\\pi } \\\\\n&= 4(\\pi  - \\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{8\\pi }{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119599 :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf r (t) = \\langle \\sin t,\\: \\cos t, \\: t \\rangle$\nfrom $t =0$ to $t = 2\\pi$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1837/Source/Images/3fca46c2b71edab0ded0e3d361c48c4f.png)"] [17592186119599 :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr^{\\prime }(t) &= \\langle \\frac{d}{dt}(\\sin t), \\frac{d}{dt}(\\cos t), \\frac{d}{dt}(t)\\rangle  \\\\\n&= \\langle \\cos t,-\\sin t, 1\\rangle  \\\\\n\\Vert r^{\\prime }(t)\\Vert  &= \\sqrt{(\\cos t)^{2} + (-\\sin t)^{2} + 1^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\cos^{2} t + \\sin^{2} t + 1} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{1 + 1} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL &= \\int _{0}^{2\\pi }\\Vert r^{\\prime }(t)\\Vert dt \\\\\n&= \\int _{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2}dt \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2}t \\mid _{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2}(2\\pi  - 0) \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{2}\\pi \n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186117731 17592186117732 17592186117733 17592186117734 17592186117735 17592186117749 17592186117750 17592186117751 17592186117752 17592186117753 17592186117785 17592186117786 17592186117787 17592186117788 17592186117789 17592186119200 17592186119201 17592186119202 17592186119203 17592186119204] "immutable_fields" [[17592186117730 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117730 :answer-field/id] [17592186117730 :answer-field/key] [17592186117730 :answer-field/type] [17592186117748 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117748 :answer-field/id] [17592186117748 :answer-field/key] [17592186117748 :answer-field/type] [17592186117784 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117784 :answer-field/id] [17592186117784 :answer-field/key] [17592186117784 :answer-field/type] [17592186119199 :answer-field/correct] [17592186119199 :answer-field/id] [17592186119199 :answer-field/key] [17592186119199 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
